# Local dev/testing only — customers never see or touch this file. The shipped Argus.exe reads
# config.json (written by the Settings UI) and falls back to the defaults below; every var here is
# just an env-var override of the same config.json keys, for running from source without one.
# Copy to .env and `bun run dev` picks it up automatically. See src/bootstrap/config.ts for the
# authoritative list of what's actually read.
PORT=58070
DATA_DIR=./data
LOG_LEVEL=info
INSTANCE_NAME=Argus

# Optional: where this instance checks for new versions (Settings → General → "Update check URL").
# Point it at your update-feed.json (see README §7 "enable auto-update"). Leave unset to disable.
# UPDATE_CHECK_URL=https://example.com/argus/update-feed.json

# --- Saas mode (M0+, see BLUEPRINT.md/SAAS_GAPS.md) — uncomment to run the multi-tenant/Postgres
# deployment instead of the default single-tenant exe-mode above. `docker compose up -d` sets
# these automatically; only needed here for running saas mode from source without Docker.
# MODE=saas
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://argus:argus_dev_password@localhost:55432/argus
# REDIS_URL=redis://localhost:56379
